The Send message button on the contact page now runs the full width of the form fields, on desktop and phone. I added this rule to `site/css/components.css`:

```css
#contact-form > .btn {
  display: flex;
  width: 100%;
}
```

- **Functional tests:** all 16 pass.
- **Visual tests:** the two contact-page screenshot comparisons (desktop and phone) now fail, because the approved screenshots still show the narrow button. The diff images show the button is the only thing that changed. I did not update the approved screenshots, so say if you want them regenerated.
- **Rule scope:** my first version targeted `.form > .btn`. That also stretched the home page's newsletter Subscribe button, because that form shares the `form` class. The home screenshots failed, so I narrowed the rule to `#contact-form`. Home matches its approved screenshots again.

STATUS: DONE

